  "body": "1,123 m² of freehold land in the heart of Campbells Bay\r\n\r\nA morning swim at Campbells Bay Beach, a long lunch on the covered patio, then dinner at El Greco. With the beach and El Greco both within a five-minute walk, summer at 7 Cloverly Crescent is looking pretty good.\r\n\r\nTucked away at the end of a cul-de-sac, this single-level home has 2.7 m ceilings, tall doors and fresh paint inside and out. The kitchen and dining area sit between the family room and a separate lounge, giving everyone room to spread out. The main bedroom has an ensuite and its own private deck, and the fourth bedroom works nicely as a home office.\r\n\r\nOpen the bifolds and step straight from the family room onto the north-facing patio. There’s a sunny lawn, an established vege garden and a quiet path through the garden. The double carport and generous off-street parking leave room for the boat or caravan, and there’s a workshop and wine cellar off the garage.\r\n\r\nWhy you’ll love it\r\n- In zone for Rangitoto College, Westlake Boys’ and Westlake Girls’\r\n- Campbells Bay Beach and El Greco within a five-minute walk\r\n- 1,123 m² of freehold land (more or less) in a private cul-de-sac setting\r\n- Four bedrooms, two bathrooms and two living areas, all on one level\r\n- North-facing covered patio, sunny lawn and established gardens\r\n- Double carport, garage, workshop, wine cellar and room for the boat or caravan\r\nDevelopers and land buyers\r\nLooking for your next site in Campbells Bay? Get in touch for the property documents and come take a look at the section. Any development is subject to your own due diligence, site suitability and any required council approvals.\r\n\r\nMove in, unpack and get the barbecue going.\r\n\r\nGive Drew or Harrison a call and come see where you could spend this summer.",
